Alex created a modified version of the popular Wordle game.

There is a hidden word S and a guessed word T, both of length 5.

For each position i (0-based indexing):

If S[i] == T[i], the corresponding character in the answer string M is 'G' (Green).

Otherwise, the corresponding character in M is 'B' (Black).

Given the hidden word S and the guessed word T, determine the string M.

Input Format
The first line contains a string S and the second line contains a string T.

Both strings consist of uppercase English letters and have a length of 5.

Output Format
Print the string M representing the correctness of each guessed character.

Sample Input

ABCDE
EDCBA

Sample Output
BBGBB




#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n=5;
    string S,T;
    cin>>S>>T;
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        if(S[i]!=T[i]){
            cout<<'B';
        }
        else{
             cout<<'G';
        }
    }
    return 0;
}
